  "grammar": [
    {
      "title": "'I have a headache': the experiencer construction",
      "body": "Physical and mental states are things that **happen to** you, so the person goes into the **dative** (-ಗೆ) and the illness or feeling is the subject:\n• ನನಗೆ ಜ್ವರ ಇದೆ 'to me fever is' = I have a fever\n• ನನಗೆ ನೆಗಡಿ ಆಗಿದೆ 'to me a cold has happened' = I've caught a cold\n• ನನಗೆ ಸುಸ್ತಾಗಿದೆ 'to me tiredness has happened' = I'm tired\n\nWith a **body part** as subject, use ನೋಯು 'hurt' in the continuous: ತಲೆ ನೋಯ್ತಿದೆ 'head is hurting', or the compound noun + ಇದೆ: ಕಾಲುನೋವು ಇದೆ 'have leg pain'. The owner can be added in the genitive or dative: ನನ್ನ ಕಾಲು ನೋಯ್ತಿದೆ / ನನಗೆ ಕಾಲು ನೋಯ್ತಿದೆ.\n\n**ಆಗು** *āgu* 'become, happen' is the key verb for changes of state: ಏನಾಯ್ತು? 'what happened?', ಗಾಯ ಆಯ್ತು 'got hurt', ಹುಷಾರಾಗಿದ್ದೀನಿ 'I've got better'.",
      "examples": [
        { "native": "ಅವನಿಗೆ ಕೆಮ್ಮು ಇದೆ", "roman": "avanige kemmu ide", "en": "He has a cough." },
        { "native": "ನನ್ನ ಬೆನ್ನು ನೋಯ್ತಿದೆ", "roman": "nanna bennu nōytide", "en": "My back hurts." },
        { "native": "ಮಗುವಿಗೆ ಜ್ವರ ಬಂದಿದೆ", "roman": "maguvige jvara bandide", "en": "The baby has a fever." },
        { "native": "ಕೈಗೆ ಗಾಯ ಆಯ್ತು", "roman": "kaige gāya āytu", "en": "I hurt my hand. (lit. a wound happened to the hand)" },
        { "native": "ಈಗ ಹುಷಾರಾಗಿದ್ದೀನಿ", "roman": "īga huṣārāgiddīni", "en": "I'm better now." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "'Should / must': verb + -ಬೇಕು, and -ಬಾರದು 'must not'",
      "body": "Add **-ಬೇಕು** to the **infinitive stem** of a verb (stem + -ಅ) to say 'must, have to, should': ಮಾಡು → ಮಾಡಬೇಕು 'must do', ಹೋಗು → ಹೋಗಬೇಕು 'must go', ತಿನ್ನು → ತಿನ್ನಬೇಕು, ಕುಡಿ → ಕುಡಿಯಬೇಕು, ಇರು → ಇರಬೇಕು. It doesn't change for person: ನಾನು / ನೀವು / ಅವರು ಹೋಗಬೇಕು.\n\nThe negatives:\n• **-ಬಾರದು** *-bāradu* 'must not, shouldn't': ತಿನ್ನಬಾರದು 'mustn't eat'\n• **-ಬೇಕಾಗಿಲ್ಲ** *-bēkāgilla* 'needn't': ಬರಬೇಕಾಗಿಲ್ಲ 'you needn't come'\n• **-ಬೇಡ** (as a command) 'don't': ತಿನ್ನಬೇಡಿ 'don't eat (polite)'\n\n'It's good to...' uses the verbal noun -ಉವುದು (spoken -ಓದು) + ಒಳ್ಳೆಯದು: ನೀರು ಕುಡಿಯುವುದು ಒಳ್ಳೆಯದು / ನೀರು ಕುಡಿಯೋದು ಒಳ್ಳೇದು 'drinking water is good'.",
      "examples": [
        { "native": "ನೀವು ಡಾಕ್ಟರನ್ನ ನೋಡಬೇಕು", "roman": "nīvu ḍākṭaranna nōḍabēku", "en": "You should see a doctor." },
        { "native": "ತುಂಬಾ ನೀರು ಕುಡಿಯಬೇಕು", "roman": "tumbā nīru kuḍiyabēku", "en": "You must drink lots of water." },
        { "native": "ಖಾರ ತಿನ್ನಬಾರದು", "roman": "khāra tinnabāradu", "en": "You shouldn't eat spicy food." },
        { "native": "ನಾಳೆ ಆಫೀಸಿಗೆ ಹೋಗಬೇಕಾಗಿಲ್ಲ", "roman": "nāḷe āphīsige hōgabēkāgilla", "en": "You needn't go to the office tomorrow." },
        { "native": "ಚೆನ್ನಾಗಿ ನಿದ್ದೆ ಮಾಡೋದು ಒಳ್ಳೇದು", "roman": "chennāgi nidde māḍōdu oḷḷēdu", "en": "Sleeping well is good for you." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "dialogue": {
    "title": "At the clinic",
    "setting": "Mark visits a neighbourhood doctor in Jayanagar.",
    "lines": [
      { "speaker": "Doctor", "native": "ಬನ್ನಿ, ಕೂತ್ಕೊಳ್ಳಿ. ಏನಾಯ್ತು?", "roman": "banni, kūtkoḷḷi. ēnāytu?", "en": "Come, sit down. What's the matter?" },
      { "speaker": "Mark", "native": "ಎರಡು ದಿನದಿಂದ ಜ್ವರ ಇದೆ, ಡಾಕ್ಟರ್.", "roman": "eraḍu dinadinda jvara ide, ḍākṭar.", "en": "I've had a fever for two days, doctor." },
      { "speaker": "Doctor", "native": "ತಲೆನೋವು, ಕೆಮ್ಮು ಇದೆಯಾ?", "roman": "talenōvu, kemmu ideyā?", "en": "Do you have a headache or a cough?" },
      { "speaker": "Mark", "native": "ತಲೆನೋವು ಇದೆ. ಗಂಟಲು ಕೂಡ ನೋಯ್ತಿದೆ.", "roman": "talenōvu ide. gaṇṭalu kūḍa nōytide.", "en": "I have a headache. My throat hurts too." },
      { "speaker": "Doctor", "native": "ಬಾಯಿ ತೆಗೀರಿ... ಸರಿ, ಸ್ವಲ್ಪ ಇನ್ಫೆಕ್ಷನ್ ಇದೆ.", "roman": "bāyi tegīri... sari, svalpa inphekṣan ide.", "en": "Open your mouth... Okay, there's a slight infection." },
      { "speaker": "Doctor", "native": "ಈ ಮಾತ್ರೆ ದಿನಕ್ಕೆ ಮೂರು ಸಲ ಊಟ ಆದಮೇಲೆ ತಗೊಳ್ಳಿ.", "roman": "ī mātre dinakke mūru sala ūṭa ādamēle tagoḷḷi.", "en": "Take this tablet three times a day after meals." },
      { "speaker": "Mark", "native": "ಏನು ತಿನ್ನಬಾರದು?", "roman": "ēnu tinnabāradu?", "en": "What shouldn't I eat?" },
      { "speaker": "Doctor", "native": "ತಣ್ಣಗಿರೋದು, ಖಾರ ಬೇಡ. ಬಿಸಿ ನೀರು ಕುಡೀರಿ, ವಿಶ್ರಾಂತಿ ತಗೊಳ್ಳಿ.", "roman": "taṇṇagirōdu, khāra bēḍa. bisi nīru kuḍīri, vishrānti tagoḷḷi.", "en": "Nothing cold or spicy. Drink hot water and rest." },
      { "speaker": "Mark", "native": "ಸರಿ ಡಾಕ್ಟರ್, ಧನ್ಯವಾದ.", "roman": "sari ḍākṭar, dhanyavāda.", "en": "Okay doctor, thank you." },
      { "speaker": "Doctor", "native": "ಬೇಗ ಹುಷಾರಾಗಿ!", "roman": "bēga huṣārāgi!", "en": "Get well soon!" }
    ]
  },
  "culture": "Home remedies are popular: ಕಷಾಯ (a hot decoction of pepper, ginger, coriander and tulsi) for colds, and ಅರಿಶಿನ (turmeric) in hot milk. Elders will advise avoiding 'cold' foods like curd and bananas during a cough. Pharmacies (ಮೆಡಿಕಲ್ ಶಾಪ್) are everywhere, and pharmacists often give advice for minor ailments.",
